        {
            "number": 5,
            "revision": "b5e2cb0ae1a5750b1d4895bcfacd1727638609e1",
            "parents": [
                "d95de99fb8fa23c40828a3bb7632c0bd224ba331"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/69/83869/5",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Alex-TS-Wang",
                "email": "alex.ts.wang@fii-foxconn.com",
                "username": "Alex-TS-Wang"
            },
            "createdOn": 1758688607,
            "author": {
                "name": "Alex-TS-Wang",
                "email": "alex.ts.wang@fii-foxconn.com",
                "username": "Alex-TS-Wang"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "What does it mean to \"retrieve a specific FRU ID\"?  It looks like we're giving them an index only?  What is this used for?\n\nWhy does the BIOS want/need to do this?  I'm surprised they would want to know raw i2c address information of the platform."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alex-TS-Wang",
                        "email": "alex.ts.wang@fii-foxconn.com",
                        "username": "Alex-TS-Wang"
                    },
                    "message": "When the BIOS reads the FRU, there are two Bianca entries, and the BIOS cannot tell which FRU ID corresponds to the first or the second Bianca FRU. This OEM command uses the I2C bus and slave address as parameters to clearly map which FRU ID comes from which Bianca."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I'd like to call this something other than \"FRU ID\" because that is very overloaded.  5 years from now we're not going to remember this conversation and why this FRU ID means \"index into an entity-manager object list\".  Can we come up with a name less generic than \"FRU ID\"?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Or... is this related to some IPMI concept of a \"FRU ID\"?  Can we related it to a different set of commands as they match?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alex-TS-Wang",
                        "email": "alex.ts.wang@fii-foxconn.com",
                        "username": "Alex-TS-Wang"
                    },
                    "message": "Is it acceptable if I add explanations about the IPMI commands related to FRU ID and indicate the source?"
                }
            ],
